  "about": "Launch weather rules, word for word as NASA publishes them for Falcon 9 at Cape Canaveral and Kennedy. rule_class is this project's classification of how a rule can be checked: 'model' from a forecast model's numbers (P = k of N ensemble runs), 'proxy' when a model can only show the ingredients, 'observation' when only an observation at the time can decide. variable names what a rule is about. Only Falcon 9's own limits are published; the lightning rules are the range's and are taken to apply to every vehicle there (stated per record). A limit a vehicle maker does not publish is entered by the team, never filled in here.",
